column16:
In 2000 there were 24,594 census blocks in Chicago from which a robber chooses a single one when committing a robbery.
   The data further include detailed information on land use, population and activities in all census blocks in the city of Chicago. In 2000, there were 24,736 census blocks in Chicago. The 142 blocks that had no land were excluded from the analysis. The remaining 24,594 blocks have a median size of 19,680 m 2 ($140 m Â 140 m).
   the complete estimation procedure involved the following steps:3 1. From the 12,938 robberies, select a random sample of 6000 robberies; 2. For each of these 6000 robberies involving multiple offenders, select a random offender from those involved;4 3. For each of the 6000 robberies, select the block where the robbery was actually perpetrated, and add to this a random sample of 5999 blocks of the other 24,593 census blocks;

